Warm up Defender scan during Windows install

Purpose: the first launch of a fresh install takes ~6.8 s instead of
~2.3 s, because Defender scans a binary on its first execution. Move
that wait into the installer's progress bar.

Approach: an Inno [Run] step starts rnote.exe --help hidden and waits.
Only real execution satisfies the scan: Start-MpScan does not, and a
byte-identical copy pays again (the verdict is cached per file).
Stripping debug symbols (218 -> 21 MB) changed nothing.

Constraints: relocates the cost, does not remove it; code signing is
the real fix. The step must exit on its own (--help does).

